course: dictionary
lesson: 11860
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words are spelled the same but mean different things. Bologna with a capital B is a place: a city in Italy. Bologna with a small b is a food: a large smoked sausage.
explain: Context tells you which one. «We drove to Bologna on our holiday in Italy.» The capital letter and the word holiday show it is the city. «My sandwich had slices of bologna in it.» The words sandwich and slices show it is the food.
explain: Check by swapping in your meaning. A city cannot be sliced thinly for lunch, so bologna in that sentence must be the sausage. Always ask: does my meaning still make sense in the sentence?
fact: Bologna with a capital B is a city in northern Italy.
fact: The city is famous for its old university and its food.
fact: Spaghetti bolognese, pasta with a meat sauce, is named after the city.
fact: Bologna with a small b is a large smoked sausage of pork and beef, sliced thinly for sandwiches.
fact: In some places it is also called «baloney» or «boloney», and in slang «baloney» can mean nonsense.
exercise: «We flew to Bologna to see its famous old university.» What is Bologna here? | A sausage sliced for lunch | A sandwich shop | A kind of pasta | *A city in Italy
exercise: «My packed lunch had slices of bologna in a sandwich.» What is bologna here? | Nonsense | *A large smoked sausage | A city in northern Italy | A grey, wet day
exercise: «Spaghetti bolognese» is named after which place? | A packed lunch | *Bologna, a city in Italy | Rome, the capital city | A large smoked sausage
test: «Bologna is famous for its old university and its food.» What does Bologna mean in this sentence? | *A city in northern Italy | A kind of sausage | A sandwich | Nonsense
test: «That story is baloney, you made it up!» What does baloney mean here? | A city in Italy | A packed lunch | *Nonsense | A large smoked sausage
exam: «We packed bologna sandwiches for our trip to Bologna.» What does the second bologna mean? | Nonsense | A large smoked sausage | A kind of pasta | *A city in northern Italy
